  "goodToKnow": "Die Klamotten are clothes, in casual German: Ich muss meine Klamotten waschen. The word is almost always plural; the neutral words are die Kleidung or die Sachen. In the singular, eine Klamotte is a slapstick comedy film or play. The origin is uncertain; it may come from a Berlin word for rubble or junk. Alte Klamotten means old clothes, or old stuff in general."
